// BT-3766: ADR 0130 Phase 0 gate 4 with the restore arm taken. A class-side
// `on:do:` in a loop whose protected block always raises, run inside an
// invocation of a class with class variables, so `snapshot/0` answers the live
// `{Key, Map}` and every iteration runs `restore/1` in the catch arm.
// `SsbOnDoRaiseObject` is the same loop outside any invocation (`snapshot/0`
// answers `none`, so `restore/1` does nothing).

Object subclass: SsbOnDoRaiseClass
  classState: hits = 0

  class loop: n :: Integer -> Integer =>
    1 to: n do: [:i | [Error signal: "x"] on: Error do: [:e | 0]]
    n
